        "title": "Cartography - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is structurally analogous to compilation. You start with a rich, multi-dimensional source (the world) and apply a series of lossy transformations to produce a target artifact optimized for a specific use case (navigation, analysis, argument). The chain is: measurement → projection → abstraction → symbolization → rendering. Change any parameter and you get a different artifact from the same source."
    }
